<!-- this preview was written by Chrissy Safranski at/after the 2024 Doenet workshop -->


  <p>
    Let 
    <me>
      T(x) = 3 - x + \frac{1}{3}x^2 - \frac{1}{9}x^3 + \cdots + 3 \cdot \left(- \frac{1}{3} \right)^n x^n + \cdots
    </me>
  </p>

  <p>
    <ol marker="a.">
      <li>
        <p>
          Show that <m>T(x)</m> is a geometric series by identifying the values of <m>a</m> and <m>r</m>.</p>
         <p> 
           <m>a=</m><answer>3</answer> 
        </p>
        <p>
          <m>r=</m><answer>-1/3*x</answer>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Use the formula for the value of the sum of an infinite geometric series to find a single fraction that is equivalent to <m>T(x)</m> when the infinite series converges. 
        </p>
        <p>
          <m>T(x) = </m> <answer>3/(1+1/3x)</answer> 
        </p>
        <p>
          For which values of <m>x</m> is this representation valid? Use interval notation to express your answer. 
        </p>
        <p>
          <m>T(x)</m> converges for all <m>x</m> in the interval <answer>(-3,3)</answer>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Now consider the function <m>f(x) = 9 (3 + x)^{-1}</m>.  Complete the following table to determine the necessary information to form <m>T_3(x)</m>, the degree <m>3</m> Taylor polynomial of <m>f(x)</m> centered at <m>a = 0</m>.
          <tabular>
                <row>
                  <cell><m>f(x)=9(3+x)^{-1}</m></cell>
                  <cell><m>f(0)=</m><answer>3</answer></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <cell><m>f'(x)=</m><answer>-9(3+x)^(-2)</answer></cell>
                  <cell><m>f'(0)=</m><answer>-1</answer></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <cell><m>f''(x)=</m><answer>18(3+x)^(-3)</answer></cell>
                  <cell><m>f''(0)=</m><answer>2/3</answer></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <cell><m>f'''(x)=</m><answer>-54(3+x)^(-4)</answer></cell>
                  <cell><m>f'''(0)=</m><answer>-2/3</answer></cell>
                </row>
              </tabular> State the degree <m>3</m> Taylor polynomial centered at <m>0</m> for the function <m>f(x)</m>. 
        </p>
        <p>
          <m>T_3(x) = </m><answer>3-x+1/3x^2-1/9x^3</answer>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          How is <m>T_3(x)</m> connected to the original series <m>T(x)</m>? 
        </p>
        <p>
          <answer>
  <choice> <m>T_3(x) = T(x)</m> for every value of <m>x</m></choice>
  <choice credit="1"><m>T_3(x)</m> is the sum of the first four terms of the infinite geometric series <m>T(x)</m>. </choice>
  <choice><m>T_3(x)</m> and <m>T(x)</m> are unrelated</choice>
</answer>   
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>